# Godavari One — Advanced Real-Time Software, APIs & Services Integration

Technology integration plan for Godavari Pushkaralu 2027

For Godavari One, I recommend building an AI-powered, real-time digital twin of the Pushkaralu event, integrated with actual map services, cameras, IoT devices, weather feeds, emergency workflows, transport GPS, and live public notifications.

The goal is to make Godavari One more than a dashboard: it should be a platform that can observe, predict, alert, coordinate, and respond.

## 1. What I found in your uploaded project

I inspected the Godavari One ZIP you uploaded.

Your project already includes eight interfaces:

- Pilgrim App
- Command Centre
- Responder App
- Field Operations
- Mobility
- Public Kiosk
- Intelligence
- Insights

It also includes crowd-risk logic, a crowd forecasting model, TensorFlow\.js components, OpenCV-inspired processing code, Leaflet maps, geofencing, family safety features, and an offline queue.

However, there is an important distinction:

| Current implementation               | What to integrate                                        |
| ------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| React + Vite frontend                | FastAPI backend and persistent database                  |
| Mock crowd and incident data         | Real-time ingestion services                             |
| Browser `localStorage`               | PostgreSQL + PostGIS                                     |
| Leaflet/OpenStreetMap map            | Live routing, traffic, GPS, geofencing                   |
| Browser-side crowd processing        | Edge video inference and authorized CCTV feeds           |
| Simulated forecasting                | Calibrated models using historical and live observations |
| Locally simulated SOS and dispatch   | Server-based incident and responder system               |
| Offline queue logic                  | Reliable server synchronization                          |
| Interface switching with local roles | Secure server-enforced authentication and RBAC           |

Your current code is a good interactive prototype, but it is not yet an operational real-time system. In particular, locally stored incidents and simulated camera activity should not be presented as genuine dispatch or CCTV monitoring.

The following integrations would turn it into a significantly more capable platform.

